Source: lliurex-access-explainer
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Eduardo Millan <eduardo.millan@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), rsync
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: lliurex-access-explainer
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, n4d, python3
Recommends: lliurex-sddm-theme
Description: Plain-language login-failure explanations for LliureX
 Shows a short, plain-language reason on the LliureX login screen when
 a student's login fails, instead of the generic "Login failed"
 message. Includes an N4D plugin (AccessExplainer) that checks SSSD
 status, local access-control lists and pam_sss logs, and a patch for
 lliurex-sddm-theme's Main.qml that asks it for that reason and shows
 it, auto-hiding after a configurable delay.
 .
 The theme patch is applied/reverted by this package's maintainer
 scripts (which just call the project's own scripts/install.sh and
 scripts/uninstall.sh), checking the installed lliurex-sddm-theme
 version and a known sha256 before touching anything, and keeping a
 backup of the original file. Re-running the patch (e.g. on a package
 reinstall) is a no-op if the file is already patched. Restarting sddm
 to apply a newly patched theme is never done automatically by this
 package.
